WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.635
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.903
and Golden Globe-nominated actor

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:05.538
you know from shows
such as "Black-ish."

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:09.041
He stars in the 21st season
of "Law &amp; Order,"

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:11.310
which premieres -- Wally?

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.813
You know what I'm going to say?

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.616
Yeah, how'd you spell
"twenty-first"?

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.551
Show everybody on the card.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:19.652
"Twent."

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.488
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:24.891
"Twent." You used
the old English spelling.

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.859
-Yeah.

00:00:26.859 --> 00:00:29.362
-"'Twas the twent-first.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.031
Oh, I remember it well.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:35.034
Four days before Christmas,
it was."

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:37.604
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:40.340
He stars --

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.876
He stars in the 21st season
of "Law &amp; Order,"

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.978
which returns
February twent-fourth.

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.846
Oh, my God.

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.115
No, I know, you got that one
right, which is weird.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.284
You would think it would be
the same on both.

00:00:51.284 --> 00:00:54.553
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:56.623
At 8:00 p.m. right here on NBC.

00:00:56.623 --> 00:00:57.656
Let's take a look.

00:00:57.656 --> 00:00:59.492
-Where were you last night,
10:00?

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.594
-At a bar in Red Hook
called Ray's.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.530
Talking to the bodyguard,
trying to work things out.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.732
-You make a deal?

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.967
-No, he offered me 50K.

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.302
Told him he can go to hell.

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.170
-Dumb move.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:12.438
-Why is that?

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:13.906
-King's dead.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:15.174
-For real, he gone?

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:16.543
-Somebody shot him.

00:01:18.577 --> 00:01:20.246
-I needed that money, man.

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:23.249
-Well, unless he named you
in his will, you're out of luck.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:26.819
-[ Chuckles ]
We'll be in touch.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:30.123
-Please welcome back to the show
Anthony Anderson, everybody.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.325
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:38.197 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:44.070 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.738
Welcome back!

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:48.040
-Thank you for having me back.
Now, before we get started --

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.409
-Yes.
-Before we get started...

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.177
-Okay.
-...you just saw in that clip

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.413
from the twent-first season
of "Law &amp; Order"...

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:57.016
-Yeah.
-...my co-star Jeffrey Donovan.

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.217
-A great actor.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:59.485
-Massachusetts guy.

00:01:59.485 --> 00:02:01.688
-Yeah, he doesn't think
you like him.

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.122
-What?

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:05.525
-Because he's been trying
to get on this show.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.159
And you guys
keep telling him no.

00:02:07.159 --> 00:02:08.394
-No, that's not true.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.597
-You just said it.
-I said it's not true.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:11.864
-Oh, okay.
I'm just letting you know.

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:13.398
-Okay.
-So I'm --

00:02:13.398 --> 00:02:14.667
Jeffrey, you heard it.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:17.737
He does like you, and he may not
need you on the show now

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:20.206
because I'm here,
but I put a plug in for you.

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:21.240
So hopefully you can
come on here.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.710
-Now, of course,
I'd have to say it

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.611
the way I just said it, right?
-Yes.

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:28.348
-I mean, if I didn't like him,
I'm not going to admit it here.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.515
-No, you're not.
-Right.

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:31.617
-No.
-So really, I think,

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:35.254
the proof will be whether or not
he's ever here.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.123
-Only time will tell.
-Yeah.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.757
-Okay.
-This is like a cliffhanger.

00:02:38.757 --> 00:02:40.526
-It is.
It is.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:42.295
-But I do.
I love Jeffrey Donovan.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:45.197
He was fantastic -- He's been
fantastic in a million things.

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:48.834
But he was fantastic in "Fargo,"
fantastic in "Burn Notice."

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:50.536
And I'm so happy to see
the two of you together.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:53.473
We were talking backstage, I'm
so happy "Law &amp; Order" is back.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.908
-No, so am I, man.

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:57.843
I didn't realize that people
really missed the mother ship.

00:02:57.843 --> 00:02:59.345
-They do.
-Yeah, yeah,

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:00.746
the way that they did, man.

00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:03.383
So, you know, people have been
stopping me on the street.

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.650
It was like, "I can't wait."

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.119
I was like, "Yeah,
season finale of 'Black-ish.'"

00:03:07.119 --> 00:03:09.288
Go, "No, not that."

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:10.723
I was like, "What,
the season premiere

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:13.459
of 'To Tell the Truth'?"
"No, not that show."

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:15.161
"What, me hosting
the Image Awards?"

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:16.963
"No! 'Law &amp; Order.'"

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:18.564
I was like, "Oh, I forgot."

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:19.731
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:19.731 --> 00:03:21.034
-I also cannot believe --

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.202
'cause you were on the last
2 1/2 seasons

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.637
of the mother ship.

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:25.705
It's been 10 years.

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.173
I can't believe
it's been 10 years.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:29.875
-Yeah, it's been
a 10-year hiatus, man.

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.912
And the appetite for the show
is still there.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.180
And that's why we're back.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.916
So I want to thank the fans
for sticking around.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:40.419
-Fantastic.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:42.388
-And you get to be back
in New York City.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.856
And I would imagine that --

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.659
You know, I think that also
"Law &amp; Order" feels like a show

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:49.862
that New Yorkers believe
they have an ownership stake in.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.163
-Yeah.
-I would imagine that

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:52.532
when you're shooting,
because, again,

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:54.100
you're shooting in the streets,
you're out and about,

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.168
people must yell at you guys all
the time when you're shooting.

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:57.036
-All the time, man.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.237
People try to get in the scenes

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.939
when we're working
on the street.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.508
You know, because we can't block
off the streets in New York

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:03.943
like we do in L.A.
or anyplace else.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.444
-Yeah.

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:06.879
-So people just walk through
the crime scene.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.214
It's like, "Hey, man, hey!

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:11.017
You're destroying evidence!
Wait a minute!"

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.685
They walk through.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:16.622
There's a photographer here that
works for the trades or whatnot,

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:18.924
man, who got into it
our very first day

00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:22.261
of our very first episode
with the AD.

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:24.330
Because we're trying
to shoot a scene,

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.266
and this guy just comes in
with the camera

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:30.536
and starts taking pictures
as if he's a part of production.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:34.172
He's just some dude -- He's just
some paparazzi dude, man.

00:04:34.172 --> 00:04:36.342
Yeah, but it's crazy.

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.977
People yell things, ruin takes,
walk through the takes.

00:04:38.977 --> 00:04:40.580
-Yeah, everybody
in New York City

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.848
also thinks they're the star
of their own TV show

00:04:42.848 --> 00:04:44.083
at any given moment.

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:45.985
They're like,
"Oh, yeah, you got a show.

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.988
I got a show, buddy.
I got a show too."

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.523
This is very exciting.
Now, be honest.

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:53.092
-Yeah.
-I know you grew up out in L.A.

00:04:53.092 --> 00:04:55.695
-Uh-huh.
-Are you a real Rams fan?

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.130
'Cause you were at
the Super Bowl, I know.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.999
-Okay, I'm going to start off
by saying I'm a sports fan.

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:01.200
-Okay, we appreciate
your honesty.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:02.501
-I'm a sports fan.

00:05:02.501 --> 00:05:05.370
I grew up wanting to play
football for the Dallas Cowboys,

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.072
'cause I thought I was
going to play football.

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:08.674
Yeah, and then --

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:10.243
Because my dad's from
Little Rock, Arkansas.

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.678
That was his team.

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:15.447
And then I got older and I
gravitated towards the Raiders.

00:05:15.447 --> 00:05:18.184
-Okay.
-And then I had friends

00:05:18.184 --> 00:05:19.985
and family who played
in the league.

00:05:19.985 --> 00:05:22.154
So I had a bunch of friends who
played for the Rams, as well.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:24.757
So I've always been a Rams fan.
It's an L.A. team.

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:27.593
And then they moved away to
St. Louis and they came back.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.094
So I am a Rams fan.

00:05:29.094 --> 00:05:30.829
-So that's wonderful.

00:05:30.829 --> 00:05:32.798
Obviously you not only
had tickets,

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:34.867
but there you are
with Matt Stafford.

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:36.669
-Yeah, on the field.
-On the field after the game.

00:05:36.669 --> 00:05:38.036
-Yeah, right after the game,
yeah.

00:05:38.036 --> 00:05:40.439
-A little --
A little sweatier than him.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.608
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.608 --> 00:05:44.143
You know, 'cause I had to --

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:46.112
I had to work my way
to get down onto the field.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.413
-Right, right.
He was just there.

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.348
-You know, he was just
effortless doing his thing.

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:50.683
That's why they're
the champions, man.

00:05:50.683 --> 00:05:53.052
So, yeah, yeah, yeah.
I was shvitzing.

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:54.787
-There you are with OBJ.

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.755
I mean, you're with
the A-listers here.

00:05:56.755 --> 00:05:59.358
-This is in the locker room
right after the game.

00:05:59.358 --> 00:06:01.293
-Then with this guy right here,
Aaron Donald,

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:03.495
arguably as good as they come.

00:06:03.495 --> 00:06:05.464
And that's Cedric, right?
-Cedric the Entertainer, yeah.

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:08.467
-That's fantastic.
And just the lack of security.

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:10.402
Here you guys are fully --

00:06:10.402 --> 00:06:12.605
I mean, 'cause I was like,
there's not --

00:06:12.605 --> 00:06:14.073
There are no Rams in this photo.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:15.441
-Yeah, yeah.
No, no.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.710
That's my best friend
Skinny Boy,

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:20.212
Ced the Entertainer, myself,
and the Lombardi, man.

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:22.515
That's how you know
you're a real fan,

00:06:22.515 --> 00:06:24.183
when they let you
in the locker room

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:26.318
and hold
the championship trophy.

00:06:26.318 --> 00:06:28.087
I'm just not no bandwagon fan.

00:06:28.087 --> 00:06:29.188
I've been there all season.

00:06:29.188 --> 00:06:30.689
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:32.825
-Genuinely I'm curious.

00:06:32.825 --> 00:06:37.396
How great is the vibe when you
are around a group of gentlemen

00:06:37.396 --> 00:06:38.564
who have just won
the Super Bowl?

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:40.333
What is it like?

00:06:40.333 --> 00:06:43.335
-Man, they were like kids
in the candy store.

00:06:43.335 --> 00:06:46.538
You know, just -- And Ced
and my buddy Jerry and I,

00:06:46.538 --> 00:06:50.610
we were the only civilians
in the locker room, literally.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:53.346
After the whistle goes off,

00:06:53.346 --> 00:06:56.649
they do the on-field
presentation of the trophy.

00:06:56.649 --> 00:06:58.050
Everybody's back
in the locker room.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.351
And it was just us, man.

00:06:59.351 --> 00:07:03.955
And it was just crazy
seeing these champions, man,

00:07:03.955 --> 00:07:05.858
and guys that I know,

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:09.061
friends of mine, you know, hoist
this trophy, smoking cigars

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.163
and having fun.

00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:12.531
So, yeah, you can't describe it.

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:13.632
Words can't begin
to describe that.

00:07:13.632 --> 00:07:15.334
-Yeah, 'cause it's that moment

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.069
where you're around
a forever thing, right?

00:07:17.069 --> 00:07:18.504
They're just going to be
champions forever.

00:07:18.504 --> 00:07:19.738
And what cool thing
to be around.

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:23.242
-Yeah, so I want to shout out
my boy O'Malley

00:07:23.242 --> 00:07:25.410
and Stan Kroenke,
the owner of the Rams,

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:26.679
for giving me that access.

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:28.046
I appreciate you guys
and I love you.

00:07:28.046 --> 00:07:29.648
-Very smart.
I saw what you did there.

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:31.950
That was very smart, 'cause
they're watching right now

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.453
like, "Why were they
in the locker room?"

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:36.088
-They know why I was
in the locker room.

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:38.190
But I just want to shout them
out on national television,

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:41.827
let them know that I --
Thank you. I love you guys.

00:07:41.827 --> 00:07:43.161
-Hey, congratulations, as well.

00:07:43.161 --> 00:07:44.896
We're talking about a new
beginning with "Law &amp; Order."

00:07:44.896 --> 00:07:46.798
Congratulations on "Black-ish."

00:07:46.798 --> 00:07:49.335
What an incredible run.
What a very special show.

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:50.970
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:53.705
-And, you know, we recently --

00:07:53.705 --> 00:07:55.574
we recently had
Tracee Ellis Ross here,

00:07:55.574 --> 00:07:58.844
and, you know, you guys
are obviously such a --

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:00.412
you know,
the leads of that show,

00:08:00.412 --> 00:08:02.815
and you play such a believable,
loving couple.

00:08:02.815 --> 00:08:04.450
What was it like
when you guys first met?

00:08:04.450 --> 00:08:05.885
Did you have chemistry
right away?

00:08:05.885 --> 00:08:08.087
-Ohhh.

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:10.323
We had chemistry
like oil and water.

00:08:10.323 --> 00:08:11.657
-Alright.
That's interesting.

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:14.693
-Yeah, we were hosting something
called the Vibe Awards

00:08:14.693 --> 00:08:16.095
like 17 years ago.

00:08:16.095 --> 00:08:17.129
-Oh, that's a while.

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.864
-Yeah, we were co-hosting it
together.

00:08:18.864 --> 00:08:21.100
And it was my first time
really hanging out with Tracee.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:24.170
And for the first half
of the show, we were great.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:25.771
We came back
from a commercial break.

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:30.275
And we're walking downstage
and you hear [Revs]

00:08:30.275 --> 00:08:31.677
And I'm with the mic.

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.212
And I just turned and said,
"Tracee, did you just fart?"

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.513
[ Laughter ]

00:08:34.513 --> 00:08:36.448
See, you laughed.
It's funny, right?

00:08:36.448 --> 00:08:38.150
I thought it was a funny joke.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.452
We know she didn't fart.
We know it was that --

00:08:40.452 --> 00:08:43.122
She hated me for 15 years.
-Yeah, well...

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:46.892
-She almost didn't come in
to read for the role of Rainbow

00:08:46.892 --> 00:08:48.961
because of her disdain for me.

00:08:48.961 --> 00:08:51.330
-Wow!
-Yeah. Yeah, but she came in.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:54.099
And it was magic,
and I had no idea --

00:08:54.099 --> 00:08:56.101
I had no idea
until the second season

00:08:56.101 --> 00:08:59.238
that she really hated me
for all those years.

00:08:59.238 --> 00:09:01.106
-Really?
-I had no idea.

00:09:01.106 --> 00:09:03.575
-She waited a full season
before she came clean?

00:09:03.575 --> 00:09:05.778
-Yeah, we were sitting there
talking and just sharing.

00:09:05.778 --> 00:09:07.513
And she came across a picture.

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:08.547
I wish I had known.

00:09:08.547 --> 00:09:09.915
I would have brought
this picture.

00:09:09.915 --> 00:09:13.452
It was a picture of us.
And I'm happy after the show.

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:16.855
After the -- the award show,
the Vibe Awards show.

00:09:16.855 --> 00:09:18.958
And I'm hugging Tracee
and I'm just cheesing.

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:21.560
And the look of disgust
on her face.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.296
And she's holding my wrist like,

00:09:23.296 --> 00:09:25.897
"Get off of me,
you disgusting man."

00:09:25.897 --> 00:09:27.833
And she showed that picture
and she told the story.

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:29.602
And I was like,
"Wow, for all these years,

00:09:29.602 --> 00:09:31.336
I thought we were friends."

00:09:31.336 --> 00:09:33.639
-Well, now you are again,
full circle.

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:34.906
-Now it comes full circle.

00:09:34.906 --> 00:09:36.141
-And "To Tell the Truth"
is back.

00:09:36.141 --> 00:09:38.343
And one of the greatest elements
about this show --

00:09:38.343 --> 00:09:40.312
talk about real chemistry --
your mom.

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:42.047
-Me and my mom.
-Your mom makes a frequent --

00:09:42.047 --> 00:09:44.082
frequent appearances
on the show.

00:09:44.082 --> 00:09:45.817
-We can't do the show
without my mother.

00:09:45.817 --> 00:09:47.786
-Does your mom enjoy her time
on-camera?

00:09:47.786 --> 00:09:49.455
-She does.

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:52.624
Little known fact -- My mother
always wanted to be an actor.

00:09:52.624 --> 00:09:54.827
-Okay.
-Yeah, she's horrible.

00:09:54.827 --> 00:09:57.596
That's why it never happened.

00:09:57.596 --> 00:10:01.099
But she -- you know, she put her
dream of being an actor on hold

00:10:01.099 --> 00:10:03.135
to raise an actor, not knowing
that's what she was doing.

00:10:03.135 --> 00:10:07.039
So for me to be in the position
that I'm in today

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:09.708
to allow her to blossom and live
out her fantasy and her dreams

00:10:09.708 --> 00:10:11.143
is truly a blessing.

00:10:11.143 --> 00:10:13.646
-And I know that she's always
been intensely proud of you.

00:10:13.646 --> 00:10:15.981
Is it true that
she used to hand out,

00:10:15.981 --> 00:10:17.583
like, signed headshots of you?

00:10:17.583 --> 00:10:19.117
-Used to?
-Okay.

00:10:19.117 --> 00:10:20.319
-She still does, Seth.

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:22.888
-Now, are these headshots
that you have signed?

00:10:22.888 --> 00:10:23.956
-No, Seth.
-Okay.

00:10:23.956 --> 00:10:27.960
-Yeah, back when
there was a Kinko's,

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:31.897
my mother would go in and forge
my signature on a headshot

00:10:31.897 --> 00:10:33.999
and go get a gross made.

00:10:33.999 --> 00:10:35.968
For those of you who don't know
what a gross is,

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:38.237
that's thousands of pictures.

00:10:38.237 --> 00:10:40.005
And so she would spend
all this money.

00:10:40.005 --> 00:10:45.377
So she has boxes of forged
autographed pictures of me

00:10:45.377 --> 00:10:47.279
in her house that she just walks
down the street --

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:49.281
"Anthony wanted you
to have this."

00:10:49.281 --> 00:10:51.984
She just hands them out
to strangers still to this day.

00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:53.118
-I can't believe that --

00:10:53.118 --> 00:10:55.354
All you had to do
was sign one once

00:10:55.354 --> 00:10:56.655
if she was taking them
to Kinko's.

00:10:56.655 --> 00:10:58.357
-Yeah, no, she did it because --

00:10:58.357 --> 00:11:00.392
She's, "Mm. Mm."

00:11:00.392 --> 00:11:01.993
She calls me "Antny."

00:11:01.993 --> 00:11:03.162
So she didn't even
write "Anthony."

00:11:03.162 --> 00:11:06.332
She wrote "Antny."
"Antny Anderson."

00:11:06.332 --> 00:11:08.400
So those are
collector's items, guys.

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.669
-If you have an original
Antny Anderson, that is --

00:11:10.669 --> 00:11:13.104
get that on eBay today.

00:11:13.104 --> 00:11:14.339
Hey, congratulations.

00:11:14.339 --> 00:11:15.807
We're so happy to have you back
in New York City.

00:11:15.807 --> 00:11:17.343
Thank you so much.
-Thanks for having me, Seth.

00:11:17.343 --> 00:11:19.311
Pleasure.
-Anthony Anderson, everybody.

00:11:19.311 --> 00:11:21.747
"Law &amp; Order" returns
February 24th

00:11:21.747 --> 00:11:23.249
at 8:00 here on NBC.

